# Tests — mandatory gate before push

After ANY change to files in `scripts/` (or to `tests/` itself):

1. Run the headless test suite from the project root:
   `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tests/run_tests.ps1`
2. All asserts must pass (`ALL TESTS GREEN`, exit code 0).
3. If anything fails: fix the code (or, if the change intentionally alters
   behavior, update the affected test and say so explicitly in the commit
   message), then re-run until green.
4. Only then commit and push (see git-push rule).

When you ADD new game mechanics or fix a logic bug, also ADD a test for it
in `tests/test_runner.gd` — a `check(...)` assert in the matching `_test_*`
function, or a new `_test_*` function wired into `_run_all()`. Keep tests
deterministic: no reliance on `randf()` outcomes, no real-time waits.

The suite backs up and restores `user://` save files itself — it is safe
to run on a dev machine. Never disable or skip it to "save time".
